    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n69984" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νέᾰτος</span></b>  (B), <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">η</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, poet. (post-<i><span class="en">
			Hom.
		</span></i>) 
			Sup. of
		
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νέος,</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>latest, last,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ν. γέννημα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Ant.</u>
					627
				</span></i>
			 (anap.); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰν ν. ὁδὸν στείχουσαν, ν.
				δὲ φέγγος λεύσσουσαν</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				807
			</span></i> (lyr.); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τίς ἄρα νέατος . .
			λήξει</span>; i.e. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὥστε νέατος
				γενέσθαι,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Aj.</u>
				1185
			</span></i> (lyr.): neut. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νέατον</span> as
				Adv., <i>for the last time,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Tr.</u>
				201
			</span></i> (lyr.).</div>
